{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Forty days.</b> Rashi explained: the first day is not counted in the reckoning, because its night is not with it, as it is written ביום הזה נבקעו כל מעינות, and so forty complete days end on the 28th of Kislev. And this does not seem correct to me, for he himself wrote regarding 'a hundred and fifty days' that it is the 1st of Sivan — how so? The rains ceased on the 27th of Kislev. Therefore it seems to me that the first day is counted in the reckoning, and the rains began from the eve of the first day, for from 'ביום הזה' there is no proof, since in many places 'ביום' and 'ביום הזה' mean the night preceding it, as in 'ביום השביעי', and likewise 'כל מלאכה לא תעשו בעצם היום הזה'. According to this, the forty days end on the 27th of Kislev, and so I found in Seder Olam, and this is its language: 'ביום הזה נבקעו כל מעיינות תהום רבה ויהי הגשם על הארץ — until when? Until the 27th of Kislev. ויגברו המים מקצה חמשים ומאת יום — until when? Until the 1st of Sivan,' etc. And if so, he certainly holds that the first day is counted in the reckoning."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:13.888132009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}